\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Architecture overview of the probabilistic flow-matching model. The most significant difference between this model and the standard deterministic variant visualized in Figure~\ref {fig:det_model_architecture} is the injection of flow-time and the noise sample from the prior distribution used in the input. The model learns to predict a velocity field that transforms the noisy sample into a physically consistent future state. The extra flow-time conditioning is concatenated onto the embeddings at each start of the Space-Then-Time attention block sequence, ensuring that temporal information is cleanly available throughout the attention processes.}}{30}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fm_model_architecture}{{5.3}{30}{Architecture overview of the probabilistic flow-matching model. The most significant difference between this model and the standard deterministic variant visualized in Figure~\ref {fig:det_model_architecture} is the injection of flow-time and the noise sample from the prior distribution used in the input. The model learns to predict a velocity field that transforms the noisy sample into a physically consistent future state. The extra flow-time conditioning is concatenated onto the embeddings at each start of the Space-Then-Time attention block sequence, ensuring that temporal information is cleanly available throughout the attention processes}{figure.caption.25}{}}
